  "body": "Consider this testcase:\r\n\r\n    <a href=\"\">Click me</a>\r\n\r\nWhat should happen when clicking the link?\r\n\r\nPer spec, I think we start at  https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#following-hyperlinks and end up doing a navigation without replacement enabled, right?\r\n\r\nI _think_ that means that each click should create a new session history entry (or at least I see nothing in the navigation algorithm in this case what would make replacement enabled by the time we land in <https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#history-traversal>), but that's not what browsers do afaict.  At least not Firefox, Chrome, or Safari.\r\n\r\nSimilar for this testcase:\r\n\r\n    <div onclick=\"location.href = location.href\">Click me</div>\r\n\r\nor for simply hitting enter in the browser url bar (though that could be a history load in browsers; the spec obviously doesn't spec that UI).",
